<mxCell id="note" value="&lt;b&gt;One account per environment&lt;/b&gt; — each holds its own sign-in, authorization, data, Lambda, images, CI roles and Terraform state; nothing in one account trusts another, and no stack reads another account's state. Stacks: prod &lt;i&gt;infra/prod/account&lt;/i&gt; + &lt;i&gt;infra/prod/app&lt;/i&gt;, dev and stage &lt;i&gt;infra/&amp;lt;env&amp;gt;/{account,app}&lt;/i&gt;. Vercel env vars are scoped by target and git_branch, one set per account. Local &lt;i&gt;npm run dev&lt;/i&gt; signs in against dev's pool. Not drawn: ACM certificates for the auth domains, Vercel DNS records, the Lambda exec role (its own bucket only)." style="rounded=1;arcSize=6;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=none;strokeColor=#AAB7B8;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;fontSize=11;fontColor=#232F3E;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="240" y="1245" width="1840" height="60" as="geometry"/></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel>
</diagram>
